<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.guest.quiesces ~ graceful stop-the-world, idempotent

`lares mempalace quiesce` pauses the hooks first (stops the minting), then SIGTERM-drains the warm daemons with a bounded SIGKILL, and confirms zero holders; a second run on a quiet system reads a clean no-op. `--hold` keeps the hooks paused for a later resume.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ quiesce · hold

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`quiesce` params=`~ drain the guest`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`hold` params=`hold/true ~ drain and keep the hooks paused`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ hold

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`hold` params=`~ keep the hooks paused after the drain`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

